-- Purpose :
--           README file for Trick Memory violations reported in the logs
--
-- --=========================================================================--
The following trick memory violations can be ignored : 

1. SMCTM32: Access time violation for Read
This violation can be ignored since it is flagged when a SMC prefetch read is
aborted at end of burst

2. SMCTM30: Access time violation for Read
This violation can be ignored since it is flagged when a SMC prefetch read is
aborted at end of burst

3. SMCTM27: Maximum time limit for the burst read access has exceeded
This violation can be ignored since a prefetch read is aborted and then
followed by a fresh read to the same address giving the impression that it is
a single read. Since this read takes the burst read access time + the prefetch
abort time of 2 clocks, the trickmemory indicates that the access time has been
exceeded.

4. SMCTM31: Maximum time limit for the burst read access has exceeded
This violation can be ignored. This is due to the the nSMOEN being deasserted
after one read from memory for HSIZE > MSIZE and being asserted after the
AHB has finished reading from the internal buffer.

5. SMCTM33: Maximum time limit for the burst read access has exceeded
This violation can be ignored. Here a prefetch read with zero access time is
followed by a new burst read starting at the next address. Therefore the RTL
does a normal mode read while the trick memory expects a burst mode read.

6. SmcTM25, TM35: Maximum time limit for the Burst mode read access has exceeded
This violation can be ignored since it is flagged when a SMC prefetch read is
aborted at end of burst

7. SmcTM35 : Maximum time limit for the Burst mode read access has exceeded
This violation can be ignored since it is flagged when a SMC prefetch read is
aborted at end of burst
